<title>AUSTRALIA: Grains Council of Australia elects new president.</title>
<headline>Grains Council of Australia elects new president.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Grower organisation Grains Council of Australia has elected a new president, Queensland grain, cotton and beef producer Brendan Stewart.</p>
<p>Stewart, 30, replaced incumbent president Jeff Arney in a ballot. Stewart said he would aim to ensure grain growers had a strong and effective national representation to ensure competitive, profitable and sustainable farming.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
